WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.094 --> 00:00:04.991
It was hot work repairing that telegraph line.

2
00:00:04.992 --> 00:00:09.482
The job took all afternoon.

3
00:00:09.483 --> 00:00:14.543
Fritzy sent the telegram that evening.

4
00:00:14.544 --> 00:00:20.534
In the morning Roscoe and Cleo got ready to interview townsfolk.

5
00:00:20.535 --> 00:00:25.003
They needed to find out who cut the wire.

6
00:00:25.004 --> 00:00:28.914
"Never rush an interview," Roscoe said.

7
00:00:28.915 --> 00:00:34.679
"Get folks to trust you first. Then they'll start talking."

8
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:39.594
"Got it," Cleo said.

9
00:00:39.595 --> 00:00:42.573
They started with Zeke.

10
00:00:42.574 --> 00:00:45.734
"You're not in trouble," Roscoe said.

11
00:00:45.735 --> 00:00:48.687
"We just need to know where you were yesterday."

12
00:00:48.688 --> 00:00:52.558
"After the ice arrived," Cleo added.

13
00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:58.654
"I was in the hills," Zeke said, "panning for gold."

14
00:00:58.655 --> 00:01:01.966
"What time?" Roscoe asked.

15
00:01:01.967 --> 00:01:08.208
Zeke rubbed his chin. "From eight thirty to six."

16
00:01:08.209 --> 00:01:13.737
Roscoe wrote that down. "Eight thirty to six."

17
00:01:13.738 --> 00:01:15.923
He looked back at Zeke.

18
00:01:15.924 --> 00:01:19.595
"You seemed excited about the gold in that sack."

19
00:01:19.596 --> 00:01:24.962
"Sure!" Zeke said. "Everyone's excited about it."

20
00:01:24.963 --> 00:01:32.162
Cleo rolled her eyes. This was taking forever!

21
00:01:32.163 --> 00:01:35.852
"Did you cut the telegraph wire?" Cleo snapped.

22
00:01:35.853 --> 00:01:39.272
Zeke gasped. "No!"

23
00:01:39.273 --> 00:01:46.245
Roscoe gave her a dirty look.

24
00:01:46.246 --> 00:01:50.287
Next they met with Mayor Wayne.

25
00:01:50.288 --> 00:01:52.845
"Sorry, Mayor," Roscoe said.

26
00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:54.676
"But I have to ask.

27
00:01:54.677 --> 00:01:58.172
Where were you yesterday after the ice delivery?"

28
00:01:58.173 --> 00:02:01.707
"Let's see," the mayor said.

29
00:02:01.708 --> 00:02:05.748
"I got to my office at 8:20 or maybe 8:50.

30
00:02:05.749 --> 00:02:10.315
I had three meetings. Or was it four?"

31
00:02:10.316 --> 00:02:19.039
Roscoe wrote this down. "Eight twenty . . . eight fifty . . . three or four meetings."

32
00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:27.227
Cleo yawned. Then she stood up.

33
00:02:27.228 --> 00:02:30.160
"Did you cut the telegraph wire?"

34
00:02:30.161 --> 00:02:39.292
Mayor Wayne snorted. "Of course not!"

35
00:02:39.293 --> 00:02:42.820
Roscoe headed to the schoolhouse with Cleo.

36
00:02:42.821 --> 00:02:46.129
He felt bad enough about interviewing everyone.

37
00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:53.081
His deputy was making things even worse.

38
00:02:53.082 --> 00:02:56.911
"This time I'll ask all the questions," Roscoe said.

39
00:02:56.912 --> 00:02:59.446
"You don't have the skills it takes yet."

40
00:02:59.447 --> 00:03:08.829
"Hmph!" Cleo frowned. "I have plenty of skills."

41
00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:11.733
Annie was at the chalkboard.

42
00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:15.951
Roscoe saw math problems all over it.

43
00:03:15.952 --> 00:03:19.628
"Howdy!" Oswald waved.

44
00:03:19.629 --> 00:03:22.770
"Good afternoon, Sheriff," Annie said.

45
00:03:22.771 --> 00:03:26.691
"What can we do for you and Deputy Cleo?"

46
00:03:26.692 --> 00:03:29.355
Roscoe took off his hat.

47
00:03:29.356 --> 00:03:32.955
"Howdy, Miss Annie. We, um . . ."

48
00:03:32.956 --> 00:03:36.716
He looked into her pretty eyes.

49
00:03:36.717 --> 00:03:40.685
Suddenly he didn't know what to say!

50
00:03:40.686 --> 00:03:43.654
Cleo rolled her eyes.

51
00:03:43.655 --> 00:03:48.720
"We're wondering where you were yesterday after the ice delivery."

52
00:03:48.721 --> 00:03:55.608
Annie smiled. "We were all here, learning our ABCs and one, two, threes."

53
00:03:55.609 --> 00:03:59.179
"What time did you get here?" Cleo asked.

54
00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:05.092
Roscoe cleared his throat. "That's enough questions, Deputy!

55
00:04:05.093 --> 00:04:11.610
Miss Annie would never cut a telegraph wire."

56
00:04:11.611 --> 00:04:16.553
He and Cleo went back outside.

57
00:04:16.554 --> 00:04:21.264
"I don't think anyone from Prickly Pear cut that wire," Roscoe said.

58
00:04:21.265 --> 00:04:29.857
Cleo nodded. "I agree. But who did?"

